      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most effective way to handle the energy transition is for governments to prioritize a rapid phase-out of fossil fuels, as the scientific consensus is clear that immediate action is necessary to limit global warming to 1.5°C and avoid catastrophic climate consequences. Slowing down the transition will only perpetuate the status quo of fossil fuel dependence, exacerbating economic and social inequalities, and ultimately leading to devastating climate-related costs. A swift transition, coupled with a just transition framework, can create new economic opportunities, drive innovation, and ensure a sustainable energy future for all.",
