    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so u're saying the economic hardship is basically just a \"necessary evil\"? that feels like a pretty extreme stance to take. if a policy causes millions of people to lose their jobs or can't afford heating in the winter just to meet an arbitrary temperature goal, isn't that policy fundamentally flawed? shouldn't we be looking for a middle ground that doesn't sacrifice people's livelihoods today?",
